-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Nodes of Yesod
  Publisher   Odin Computer Graphics, 1985
  Version     1.6

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Nodes of Yesod (1985)(Odin Computer Graphics)(128K).z80
  MD5         4dd5e967592f0eabd20f113cb64f740e

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures are drawn on the Next's own graphics layers, so they keep their
  own colours and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is
  unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    Latest owner-painted sprites and matching pink/grey/orange HUD
              portrait. Exact flat colours, including deliberate black detail
              and painted interior pixels; no outside outline. Source:
              Enhanced colours: Jon Attree.

  Pace        original (+0.45% measured in JNext 1.1.104 headless on the
              NextZXOS v2.09 card, against the plain build of the same start
              state; probe 40048; both games: 144 timers ticked per update, R
              per site at 16 sites, the seconds byte at the object spawner's
              reads held to the update count, Infinite Lives; game state, 208
              addresses including all 16 object records, equal at every update
              counted)

  Changes     1.5: final owner sprite pass, 456 exact-palette pixels across 12
              mole and enemy-spaceman graphics. Only sprite patterns changed;
              HUD, code, palettes, backdrops and timing retained. 1.6: the
              game now holds the original's pace; 1.5 ran up to 3.8% fast in
              busy scenes and up to 16% slow in short stretches. Art
              unchanged.

  Note        1 keyboard; Z/X move; Q jump; A mole. Enhanced colours and
              Backdrops are independent and off by default. Backdrops select
              surface aurora or distant cavern walls automatically. Plays at
              the original's pace in JNext, 2026-11-08, same input and game
              state equal at every update, default, Enhanced and Backdrops, 4
              runs of up to 1,500 updates: overall +0.1 to +0.5%, quiet -0.2
              to +0.2%, busy 0.0 to +0.9% (1.5, same measure: overall -2.4 to
              -1.5%, busy down to -3.4%). Measured on a test fixture in both
              games. Known issues: slowest stretch of 20 updates +3.7% (one of
              284; all others within 2.1%; 1.5: +15.7%); now and then the
              player breaks up into sprite pieces during the death animation,
              clearing on respawn (not yet reproduced or fixed); the
              original's collision-loop bug remains. Missing: caverns not
              measured; the ending not checked; hardware untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Infinite time
   3  Infinite energy
   4  Drop from any height
   5  Don't get stunned
   6  Don't get bounced
   7  No alchiem stealing

